s":{"content":[{"config":{"align":"center","direction":"horizontal","gap":6},"id":"history-v1-head","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"comments.sample.date.edit"},"tone":"subtle","variant":"label","weight":"normal"},"id":"history-v1-time","type":"Text"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"comments.editCurrent"},"tone":"neutral","variant":"soft"},"id":"history-v1-current","type":"Badge"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"comments.sample.message.ownPayLabelEdited"},"tone":"default","variant":"ui"},"id":"history-v1-body","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"spacing":0},"id":"history-sep","type":"Divider"},{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":2},"id":"history-v2","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"align":"center","direction":"horizontal","gap":6},"id":"history-v2-head","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"comments.sample.date.original"},"tone":"subtle","variant":"label","weight":"normal"},"id":"history-v2-time","type":"Text"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"comments.editOriginal"},"tone":"neutral","variant":"outline"},"id":"history-v2-original","type":"Badge"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"comments.sample.message.ownPayLabel"},"tone":"default","variant":"ui"},"id":"history-v2-body","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Thread bubble: reasons, deleting and editing","spec":{"accessibility":["The delete confirmation is a group named by its title and described by its body, with focus on Cancel; its refusal and error are alerts. The editor is a text box named \"Edit message\", the edited marker names the time of the edit, and the history is a list."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Button, Badge, Icon, Avatar, TextInput, Alert); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","Each step is shown by one Variant; the history popover is a card under the bubble, and the edited marker is a Text, not the button that opens it. Date and time of each version are sample strings per Locale.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; no step's text is typed into a field by a Variant other than through a Locale key of its own.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (names); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A reader opened the bubble of a thread on the canvas and chose Duplicate…, Reopen, Delete comment or Edit; the step opens inside the bubble, where the row of the choice was, and takes focus.","The base state is the bubble of an open thread with one message written by the reader, the reply box and Resolve; the Variants show the steps, one at a time.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the bubble is Workbench chrome, so its text follows the Workbench language and is baked here per Locale. The names, messages and times are sample content."],"intent":"Show the inline steps of the thread bubble as built from Adapter Widgets only: the reason a reader gives to resolve a thread as a duplicate or to reopen it, the confirmation to delete a comment, the refusal when someone already answered, and the editing of one's own message with its edited marker and read-only history.","interactionRules":["Resolve as duplicate asks which thread this repeats first; the button stays disabled until there is a reason. Reopen asks why, optionally. Enter confirms, Esc cancels, and the request in flight disables the button with a spinner.","Delete comment is confirmed inline, never in a browser dialog: it replaces the reply box and the Resolve row with \"Delete this comment?\", says it is removed for everyone and cannot be restored, and has Cancel (focused) and Delete; the destructive color appears only here. Only the author of a thread that holds one message, still open and unanswered, may delete it; the author's own edits and moves of the pin never count as an answer.","When someone answered meanwhile, the delete is refused with \"Someone has already responded, so this comment can't be deleted. Dismiss it instead.\" and the delete offer goes away; a delete that failed for another reason says so.","Edit turns the reader's own message into a text box in place: ⌘↵ saves and Esc cancels; Save stays disabled until the text changed. An edited message says edited after its time, which opens its earlier versions, newest first, with the time of each and Current and Original marked, read-only for every reader of the thread."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a104-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a107-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a07"}],"requirements":["01a194f5-7dc3-7ab6-83e9-7fe32b76d01a"]},"variants":{"delete-busy":{"requirements":["01a11544-598c-7217-8b56-7cb8ff0236da"],"state":{"footer":{"visible":false},"retract-busy":{"visible":true}}},"delete-confirm":{"requirements":["01a11544-598c-7217-8b56-7cb8ff0236da","01a11544-59df-7822-9aba-ff39da0d826b","01a11544-5b1b-7dcb-bcea-e36f4ffa3b2a"],"state":{"footer":{"visible":false},"retract":{"visible":true}}},"delete-failed":{"state":{"delete-failed-wrap":{"visible":true},"footer":{"visible":false},"retract":{"visible":true}}},"delete-refused":{"requirements":["01a11544-59df-7822-9aba-ff39da0d826b","01a11544-5a2e-716b-9a06-c910418f24ac"],"state":{"delete-refused-wrap":{"visible":true}}},"edit-failed":{"state":{"edit-failed-wrap":{"visible":true},"m1":{"visible":false},"m1-edit":{"visible":true}}},"edit-history":{"requirements":["01a11544-5916-774b-a7e3-529bd29eb1ea","01a11544-5855-75ad-ba0c-4132b19973ec","01a11544-587e-74a3-96b8-cf85473bed0f"],"state":{"history":{"visible":true},"m1":{"visible"